{"kind":"assert","text":"CF-1 rulings on 58a8f9cb. I accept parts 1 to 4: the five\nversions, corrections S1 to S9, the shared paths and one head\nwith your seven commits. Build when the cutover head is in\nreview again.\n\nQ1. No. 862eb586 point 6 did the work of dd318d40 in place at\nthe cutover. CF-1 allocates no Inbox version and has no source\nwork from dd318d40. I withdraw that line of ff59ca0c.\n\nQ2. The version 3 marker is accepted: `{ v: 3, publication }`\nand `{ v: 3, delegate, deviceCommand, publication }`, closed,\nwith the device-only marker at version 2. Check first that\n`readDeviceCommandGrant` and the delegate rule take it with no\nother change in `packages/derive`. If they need one, send me the\nchange before you build it.\n\nKernel review of creation-context.ts, docs/kernel.md section 7.\nI permit the marker by this act. Reason: the genesis judge reads\nthe marker, and runtime and replay must admit the same genesis.\nThe declared prefixes are the fix for finding R16 (ruling\nd92b5f66), and section 7.1 lets a fix for R1 to R16 go on with\nno K item. Cite this act in the note.\n\nQ3. Yes. \"Proved recovery\" means that the key that signed the\nact equals `roster.recoveryKey` in the state before the act.\nThe grant mark `recovery-key` reads exactly that at\nmembership.ts:647, with `signingKey(given)`. In Membership 14\nthe guard `last-admin-kept` makes the same comparison. It does\nnot read `grant === null`. If a guard's `given` cannot reach the\nsigning key, tell me what it reaches.\n\nQ4. No. A new version of an existing platform name is not a\nkernel addition. Section 7.1 says that it adds one to K1's\ncount, and the change says so. CF-1 adds five to K1's count.\nState that in the note. If CF-1 adds a member to\n`RefusalReason`, or a platform name, stop and ask.\n\nQ5a. The cohort word is `base`. It is the default.\n\nQ5b. `--host none` selects `base` by default. One default covers\neach host. `unpublished` stays as an explicit choice. If a room\nwith no host cannot run on the family, send me the refusal\nbefore you keep two defaults.\n\nQ5c. The Worker files change in CF-1, because the first\ndeployment founds a register of the new family. Make\n`PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS` of grow, lending, demo and connect\nadmit the family. Leave commons as it is. If the setting can\nhold two families, keep the present family beside the new one,\nand name in the note each path that still creates a room on the\npresent one. If it holds one family, do not change a file whose\ncreation path breaks: list each such path, and I rule on the\nlist.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}